{"name":"Dancing Crocodiles","hex":"#254a47","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dancing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The activity of taking part in a dance.","A dance club in France."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of dance"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dancing"},{"term":"crocodiles","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of crocodile"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of crocodile"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crocodiles"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crocodile","blocks":[{"text":"A crocodile or true crocodile is a large, semiaquatic reptile that lives throughout the tropics in Africa, Asia, the Americas and Australia. The term \"crocodile\" is sometimes used more loosely to include all extant members of the order Crocodilia, which includes the alligators and caimans, the gharial and false gharial as well as other extinct taxa. This article uses \"crocodile\" or \"true crocodile\" to refer only to the species taxonomically included in the Crocodylidae family, extant or extinct."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Nile_crocodile_head.jpg/330px-Nile_crocodile_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile","wikidata":"Q43169"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Nile_crocodile_head.jpg/500px-Nile_crocodile_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Nile_crocodile_head.jpg/1280px-Nile_crocodile_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Nile_crocodile_head.jpg/500px-Nile_crocodile_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn